blurgtext Pyxis port

CallumDev/blurgtext 0.2.1, tag commit bfbb3df576d2df55451df7621d7e7b506dfae8fe, MIT.
The exact direct and nested submodules, FreeType 2.15.0 and HarfBuzz 15.0.0
are in metadata.lua and the installed source.txt. Raqm 0.11.0 is fetched from
canonical HOST-Oman/libraqm, without local dependency changes. All archives are fetched
through the cache and verified before use; bundled CMake uses those local bytes.

The first port retains upstream's FT -> HB -> FT static build and PNG shim.
It does not substitute Pyxis libfont. PlutoVG's upstream stb code remains its
own optional SVG/text support. A reusable FreeType/HarfBuzz package is later work.

The unchanged demo draws over native SDL2/OSMesa. The package-only Pyxis sysfonts
backend adds family/weight/italic selection and coverage fallback. It uses only
the declared fonts package. Font loading is separate from canonical registration
so synthetic/fallback instances cannot replace the family's real faces. Each
returned fallback instance is distinct because blurgtext's fallback links mutate.

Original upstream files retain their licences. The Pyxis adaptations and build
files are MPL-2.0 under pyxis-ports/LICENSE; their patches and complete modified
source files are included. SDL2/OSMesa, Mesa and SDK notices and covered backend
sources are retained separately. See ATTRIBUTION and the full adjacent notices.

No font bytes, demo text, coordinates, colours or style spans are changed.
Only SDL2/OSMesa selection, platform font paths and callback-only GL loading
are adapted in the demo. Startup/presentation/pacing/cleanup follow upstream. Assets are read from pkg://fonts, never host paths.
